From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:16:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Face Swap: steadier face tracking

Vendored Deep-Live-Cam live pipeline:

- detect_every_frame: run face detection on every frame instead of every
  ~2nd frame at 30 fps; a held detection made the face move in steps.
- stabilization (0..1): low-pass filter on the 5 alignment landmarks,
  log-mapped 20 Hz .. 4 Hz (0.5 ~ 9 Hz), reset on large jumps. Tuned on
  real 30 fps footage; a speed-adaptive One-Euro term did not help.

Landmark jitter (% of inter-ocular distance), two 10 s clips:
moving speaker 17.4 -> 6.5, still speaker 4.85 -> 3.62, for ~2 ms per
frame (~31 ms/frame total on an M3). Both default off in the library.

Face Swap tab: Stabilization slider (default 0.5) and "Detect every
frame" checkbox (default on).

Applio-Commit: f2cbf178b15363639369467b06b20db022d84891
---
 _vendor/modules/globals.py |  2 +
 _vendor/modules/live.py    | 85 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 84 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

